  user_input {
    user_response: "Must-have (the core demo flow \342\200\224 build these first)\n\nChallenge submission \342\200\224 a real form (title, description, category, district, urgency) that saves to a database and shows up in a live list. This is the \"crowdsourcing\" half of the brief.\nRole-based login \342\200\224 at minimum 2 roles: someone who posts a challenge (Citizen/Govt) and someone who solves it (Student). Shows you understood the \"collaborative\" multi-stakeholder angle.\nProposal submission \342\200\224 a student/team can view a challenge and submit a solution against it (text + optional file). i need thse feature working properly\n\nStatus tracking \342\200\224 challenge moves through states (Submitted \342\206\222 Under Review \342\206\222 Team Assigned) and this visibly updates in the UI. This alone demonstrates the full loop judges want to see.\nOne AI-powered feature, working live \342\200\224 e.g. auto-suggesting relevant categories/departments for a new challenge, or summarizing a proposal. Judges expect AI integration in 2026 \342\200\224 pick one and make it genuinely functional, not a static label.\n\nStrong to include if time allows (differentiators, not required for the loop to work)\n6. District heatmap \342\200\224 visual, Jharkhand-specific, easy to build with dummy data, and instantly shows judges \"this is built for us,\" not a generic template.\n7. Industry sponsorship / mentor matching \342\200\224 even a simple version (industry partner sees challenges tagged to their sector, can \"sponsor\" one) shows the university-industry piece isn\'t an afterthought.\n8. Multilingual toggle (Hindi) \342\200\224 even just the landing page and challenge form \342\200\224 a fast, visible accessibility win."
    items {
      text: "Must-have (the core demo flow \342\200\224 build these first)\n\nChallenge submission \342\200\224 a real form (title, description, category, district, urgency) that saves to a database and shows up in a live list. This is the \"crowdsourcing\" half of the brief.\nRole-based login \342\200\224 at minimum 2 roles: someone who posts a challenge (Citizen/Govt) and someone who solves it (Student). Shows you understood the \"collaborative\" multi-stakeholder angle.\nProposal submission \342\200\224 a student/team can view a challenge and submit a solution against it (text + optional file). i need thse feature working properly\n\nStatus tracking \342\200\224 challenge moves through states (Submitted \342\206\222 Under Review \342\206\222 Team Assigned) and this visibly updates in the UI. This alone demonstrates the full loop judges want to see.\nOne AI-powered feature, working live \342\200\224 e.g. auto-suggesting relevant categories/departments for a new challenge, or summarizing a proposal. Judges expect AI integration in 2026 \342\200\224 pick one and make it genuinely functional, not a static label.\n\nStrong to include if time allows (differentiators, not required for the loop to work)\n6. District heatmap \342\200\224 visual, Jharkhand-specific, easy to build with dummy data, and instantly shows judges \"this is built for us,\" not a generic template.\n7. Industry sponsorship / mentor matching \342\200\224 even a simple version (industry partner sees challenges tagged to their sector, can \"sponsor\" one) shows the university-industry piece isn\'t an afterthought.\n8. Multilingual toggle (Hindi) \342\200\224 even just the landing page and challenge form \342\200\224 a fast, visible accessibility win."
